  "details": "- CVE-2026-11721: reject RRSIGs whose labels field is smaller than the\n  signer name or larger than the owner name (forged wildcard records,\n  cache poisoning)\n- CVE-2026-10723: require NSEC3 records to be signed by the zone exactly\n  one label above their owner name (forged NXDOMAIN proofs)\n- CVE-2026-94300: serialize access to the shared GSS-TSIG security\n  context (memory corruption on concurrent or replayed GSS-TSIG traffic)\n- CVE-2026-19630: bound how many compression pointers a name and a\n  message may make named follow (CPU exhaustion on crafted messages)\n- CVE-2026-11622: keep the cache header that owns NOQNAME and closest\n  encloser proofs referenced while the proofs are in use (use-after-free)",
